Subject: [PATCH] hw/ide/atapi: report a CD-ROM given a model as that drive

qemu-xen e064f42c80, QEMU_UPSTREAM_REVISION of Xen 4.20.1. The Xen build
clones it into tools/qemu-xen-dir-remote; `make xen` applies this there.
docs/architecture/guest-identity.md has why.

An ide-cd given a model (-global ide-cd.model=...) reported it only in
IDENTIFY PACKET. Its INQUIRY data still said vendor "QEMU", product
"QEMU DVD-ROM", and Windows names a CD-ROM from those: the drive of a
guest installed from one stayed in its registry as
Enum\IDE\CdRomQEMU_QEMU_DVD-ROM_..., which malware reads (al-khaser
check 4097). Report the model there too, split as a real drive's is:
the vendor its first word, the product the rest.

A CD-ROM given no model answers as before.

 hw/ide/atapi.c | 35 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hw/ide/atapi.c b/hw/ide/atapi.c
index e82959d..aef7325 100644
--- a/hw/ide/atapi.c
+++ b/hw/ide/atapi.c
@@ -705,6 +705,38 @@ static void cmd_request_sense(IDEState *s, uint8_t *buf)
     ide_atapi_cmd_reply(s, 18, max_len);
 }
 
+/*
+ * The vendor and product of a drive given a model (ide-cd.model), split as a
+ * real ATAPI drive's are: the vendor is the model's first word, the product the
+ * rest. Windows names a CD-ROM from these two, not from IDENTIFY PACKET's
+ * model, so a drive given another model still showed up as "QEMU QEMU
+ * DVD-ROM" in its registry. A first word longer than the 8 characters of the
+ * vendor field gives the model's first 8 characters instead.
+ */
+static void inquiry_vendor_product(IDEState *s, uint8_t *vendor,
+                                   uint8_t *product)
+{
+    const char *model = s->drive_model_str;
+    size_t len = strlen(model);
+    const char *space = memchr(model, ' ', MIN(len, 9));
+    char name[9];
+
+    if (!strcmp(model, "QEMU DVD-ROM")) {
+        padstr8(vendor, 8, "QEMU");
+        padstr8(product, 16, "QEMU DVD-ROM");
+        return;
+    }
+
+    len = space ? (size_t)(space - model) : MIN(len, 8);
+    pstrcpy(name, len + 1, model);
+    padstr8(vendor, 8, name);
+    model += len;
+    if (*model == ' ') {
+        model++;
+    }
+    padstr8(product, 16, model);
+}
+
 static void cmd_inquiry(IDEState *s, uint8_t *buf)
 {
     uint8_t page_code = buf[2];
@@ -798,8 +830,7 @@ static void cmd_inquiry(IDEState *s, uint8_t *buf)
         buf[5] = 0;    /* reserved */
         buf[6] = 0;    /* reserved */
         buf[7] = 0;    /* reserved */
-        padstr8(buf + 8, 8, "QEMU");
-        padstr8(buf + 16, 16, "QEMU DVD-ROM");
+        inquiry_vendor_product(s, buf + 8, buf + 16);
         padstr8(buf + 32, 4, s->version);
         idx = 36;
     }
